---
title: Tags
description: Browse posts by tag.
permalink: /tags
layout: default.liquid
data:
  wide: true
pagination:
  include: Tags
  permalink_suffix: _p/{{num}}
  per_page: 10
---
{%- comment -%}
  One file, two kinds of output — this is how Cobalt's tag pagination works
  (see _reference/example-tags/):

    * /tags/            -> paginator.indexes is set: the list of every tag
    * /tags/<tag>/      -> paginator.pages is set: the posts carrying that tag

  Two traps worth knowing:
    1. paginator.index_title does NOT exist on the index page. Reading it
       there is a hard build error ("Unknown index"), so it may only be touched
       inside the else branch.
    2. A conditional test tolerates a missing paginator field (it reads as
       falsy), but interpolating one is a build error. That's why the prev/next
       block below guards on paginator.previous_index before printing the
       permalink — those fields are absent entirely when a tag has one page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% if paginator.indexes %}
<h1>Tags</h1>
<p class="site-tagline">Every tag used so far, with the number of posts under each.</p>

<ul class="tag-index">
  {%- for ptag in paginator.indexes %}
  <li>
    <a class="tag" href="/{{ ptag.index_permalink }}/">{{ ptag.index_title }}</a>
    <span class="tag-count">{{ ptag.total_pages }}</span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<h1>Tagged &ldquo;{{ paginator.index_title }}&rdquo;</h1>
<p class="site-tagline"><a href="/tags/">&#8592; All tags</a></p>

{% assign post_list = paginator.pages %}
{% include "post-list.liquid" %}

{% if paginator.total_pages > 1 %}
<nav class="pagination">
  {%- if paginator.previous_index %}
  <a href="/{{ paginator.previous_index_permalink }}/">&#8592; Newer</a>
  {%- endif %}
  <span class="pagination-position">{{ paginator.index }} / {{ paginator.total_pages }}</span>
  {%- if paginator.next_index %}
  <a href="/{{ paginator.next_index_permalink }}/">Older &#8594;</a>
  {%- endif %}
</nav>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
